[statement]
As `a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-passed-over-beside-one-depending-on-its-requirer`,
through a package further up the chain of requirements: `top` needs `b`,
`b` needs `a`, and `a` 1 needs `top`; apk passes over `a` 3, which needs
`missing`, and installs `a` 1. A dependency on a package `top` needs
beside `b`, or one reached only through another package, does not do this
(`a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-not-passed-over-for-a-package-beside-the-chain`).

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:b

P:a
V:1
D:top

P:a
V:3
D:missing

P:b
V:2
D:a

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install a 1
install b 2
install top 1
